n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/ARCHITECTURE.md` | documentation | describes current GitHub-only architecture | CONTENT_UPDATE | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/DOCUMENTATION_DRIFT_AUDIT.md` | documentation | drift audit | CONTENT_UPDATE | MEDIUM |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/README.md` | documentation | user-facing; mentions GitHub backend | CONTENT_UPDATE | MEDIUM |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/CLI_TO_MCP_MIGRATION.md` | documentation | migration guide | CONTENT_UPDATE | MEDIUM |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/github-integration.md` | documentation | explicitly GitHub-scoped behavior docs | CONTENT_UPDATE | HIGH |\\n| `.github/workflows/backlog-sync.yml` | ci | calls backlog_backlog_sync; needs backend env var | CI_UPDATE | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/github-integration.md` | agent-instruction | GitHub behavior encoded as universal | AGENT_UPDATE | HIGH |\\n| `.claude/agents/backlog-mcp-validator.md` | agent-instruction | validates MCP tools; must target specific backend | AGENT_UPDATE | HIGH |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/backlog/SKILL.md` | agent-instruction | may frame GitHub as universal | CONTENT_UPDATE | MEDIUM |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/complete-implementation/SKILL.md` | agent-instruction | GitHub-specific PR/issue closure instructions | CONTENT_UPDATE | MEDIUM |\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n- Overall system risk: **HIGH**\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 refactoring target; 271 GitHub references; every MCP operation depends on it\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests/conftest.py` \u2014 shared fixtures; if GitHub client is provisioned directly here, all 60+ test files inherit the coupling\\n  - `plugins/python3-development/scripts/migrate_tasks_to_github.py` \u2014 cross-plugin dependency with no test coverage visible; silent breakage risk\\n  - `.github/workflows/backlog-sync.yml` \u2014 production CI sync; breaks the live backlog-to-GitHub-Issues pipeline if backend env var not set\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_backlog_core_server.py` \u2014 the acceptance criteria gate; must pass unchanged for AC #6 to be met\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - **compatibility** \u2014 7+ consumers import directly from modules being reorganized\\n  - **migration** \u2014 GitHub backend must cover 100% of current operations.py surface before cutover\\n  - **verification** \u2014 cross-backend test suite (AC #5) does not yet exist; all GitHub behavior currently tested against the live implementation, not a protocol contract\\n  - **scope** \u2014 `test_backend_status.py` may contain prior partial work; `tests/test_implementation_manager/test_github_flag.py` and cross-plugin import in `python3-development` were not in original item description\\n  - **documentation** \u2014 ARCHITECTURE.md, github-integration.md, and README.md all encode GitHub behavior as universal; misleads future backend implementors\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - **cross-plugin dependency**: `plugins/python3-development/scripts/migrate_tasks_to_github.py` imports backlog_core from development-harness \u2014 not in original scope\\n  - **implementation-manager sub-system**: two scripts (`task_status_hook.py`, `implementation_manager.py`) import backlog_core internally \u2014 not in original scope\\n  - **SAM sub-system**: `sam_schema/server.py` and `sam_schema/cli.py` import from backlog_core \u2014 not in original scope\\n  - **prior abstraction work**: `test_backend_status.py` may represent prior backend abstraction exploration \u2014 must be read before designing protocol\\n  - **tests/test_implementation_manager/test_github_flag.py** \u2014 tests a GitHub-specific flag that may become the backend-selection mechanism\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved (GitHub backend must cover 100% of operations.py before any alternative backend ships)\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked (`test_backend_status.py` read for prior art before protocol design begins; cross-plugin import in python3-development scoped)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer**, I want **The backlog MCP server (10 tools, 382+ tests) is tightly coupled to GitHub Is...** so that **backlog items are tracked in GitHub**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: User request\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-02\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-02)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**Score: 9/10 \u2014 P1 recommended (upgraded from P2 8/10)**\\n\\nOriginal scoring assumed 10 MCP tools. Fact-check revealed **40 tools** across 5 operation groups (backlog, dispatch, artifact, SAM, profile). This is a 4x scope increase.\\n\\nUpgrade justification:\\n- 40 tools tightly coupled to GitHub \u2014 not 10. Abstraction surface is 4x larger.\\n- Cross-plugin callers: python3-development plugin and SAM sub-system import backlog_core directly. Breaking changes propagate beyond the plugin boundary.\\n- operations.py (~1400+ lines) imports PyGithub, gh_client, and github_sync throughout \u2014 extraction is not a simple interface swap.\\n- .github/workflows/backlog-sync.yml will break without backend configuration.\\n- 65 affected systems identified by impact analysis, 45 with confirmed dependencies.\\n\\nRisk of NOT doing this: every new tool or backend caller deepens the coupling. Cost of abstraction grows with each addition.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n**Risk: HIGH** (impact-analyst: 65 systems, 45 with yes answers)\\n\\n**Direct impact:**\\n- `operations.py` (~1400+ lines) \u2014 primary coupling point, imports PyGithub/gh_client/github_sync throughout\\n- `gh_client.py` \u2014 GitHub API client (was github.py, now split into 3 files)\\n- `github_sync.py` \u2014 sync operations between local YAML and GitHub Issues\\n- `github_branches.py` \u2014 branch-related GitHub operations\\n- `server.py` \u2014 40 MCP tool definitions, all route through operations.py\\n- `models.py` \u2014 data models (may need backend-agnostic base types)\\n\\n**Cross-plugin impact:**\\n- `python3-development` plugin imports backlog_core \u2014 interface changes break it\\n- SAM sub-system imports backlog_core \u2014 task management depends on current API\\n- `.github/workflows/backlog-sync.yml` \u2014 CI workflow assumes GitHub backend, needs backend env var\\n\\n**Test impact:**\\n- 47 test files, 279 test functions (fact-checked; original claim of 382+ was incorrect)\\n- Tests assume GitHub fixtures \u2014 backend-agnostic test suite needed\\n\\n**Blast radius mitigation:** Phase the work so each phase has a stable checkpoint. Never break the GitHub backend while building the abstraction.\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\n\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n1. **Backend portability** \u2014 all 40 MCP tools work against any conforming backend (GitHub, GitLab, Jira, SQLite, Beads)\\n2. **Offline development** \u2014 SQLite/local backend enables backlog operations without network access\\n3. **Testing isolation** \u2014 backend-agnostic test suite validates tool behavior independent of GitHub API availability and rate limits\\n4. **Ecosystem integration** \u2014 enables GSD, Superpowers, and Beads agent frameworks to use backlog tooling natively\\n5. **Reduced coupling** \u2014 operations.py loses direct PyGithub/gh_client/github_sync imports, becoming backend-agnostic orchestration\\n6. **CI resilience** \u2014 backend configuration in backlog-sync.yml allows CI to run against test backends\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\n**Given** a user configures backlog_core with any conforming backend implementation,\\n**When** they invoke any of the 40 MCP tools (backlog, dispatch, artifact, SAM, profile groups),\\n**Then** the tool produces equivalent behavior \u2014 same response shape, same side effects \u2014 regardless of which backend is active.\\n\\n**Specific expectations:**\\n- `backlog_add` creates an item in the configured backend (GitHub Issue, SQLite row, Beads node)\\n- `backlog_list` returns items from the configured backend with identical response structure\\n- `backlog_sync` synchronizes between local YAML cache and the configured backend\\n- `backlog_groom` writes groomed content to the configured backend\\n- All dispatch, artifact, SAM, and profile tools operate through the backend protocol\\n- Backend switch requires only configuration change \u2014 no code changes in skills, agents, or MCP tool definitions\\n- GitHub backend remains the default; existing users experience zero behavioral change\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] AC1: Backend protocol interface defined as Python ABC or Protocol class with methods covering all 40 MCP tool operations grouped by domain (backlog, dispatch, artifact, SAM, profile)\\n- [ ] AC2: GitHub-specific code extracted from operations.py into GitHubBackend class that implements the backend protocol, delegating to gh_client.py + github_sync.py + github_branches.py (note: github.py no longer exists \u2014 was split into these 3 files)\\n- [ ] AC3: operations.py refactored to accept a backend instance via dependency injection \u2014 zero direct imports of PyGithub, gh_client, github_sync, or github_branches at module level\\n- [ ] AC4: Backend discovery mechanism implemented (env var `BACKLOG_BACKEND` or config in pyproject.toml) with GitHub as default\\n- [ ] AC5: At least one alternative backend implemented (SQLite recommended for simplicity) proving the protocol works end-to-end\\n- [ ] AC6: All 40 MCP tools callable against any conforming backend with identical response shapes (backlog: ~15 tools, dispatch: 6 tools, artifact: 5 tools, SAM: 7 tools, profile: 2 tools)\\n- [ ] AC7: Backend-agnostic test contract suite covering all 40 tool operation groups \u2014 runs against every registered backend\\n- [ ] AC8: All 279 existing test functions still passing (verified count \u2014 original 382+ claim was incorrect)\\n- [ ] AC9: .github/workflows/backlog-sync.yml updated with backend configuration support\\n- [ ] AC10: Cross-plugin callers (python3-development, SAM sub-system) continue working without modification \u2014 public API unchanged\\n- [ ] AC11: No MCP tool signature changes \u2014 all 40 tools retain identical parameter schemas and response shapes\\n\\n### Research\\n\\n| Source | Path | Key Insight |\\n|--------|------|-------------|\\n| Beads | research/task-management/beads.md | Distributed git-backed graph tracker using Dolt (versioned SQL); bd ready for agent work queues; 17,269 stars |\\n| GSD | research/agent-frameworks/get-shit-done.md | Meta-prompting system; 11 agents, XML task format, file-based state (STATE.md, ROADMAP.md); 10,193 stars |\\n| Superpowers | research/agent-frameworks/superpowers.md | 14-skill dev workflow framework with spec-driven execution; 40,911 stars |\\n\\n### Skills\\n\\n- /backlog \u2014 main backlog interface (skill under refactoring)\\n- /python3-development \u2014 Python architecture and testing\\n- /fastmcp-creator \u2014 MCP server patterns\\n\\n### Agents\\n\\n- @python-engineering:python-cli-architect \u2014 for protocol design and implementation\\n- @python-engineering:python-pytest-architect \u2014 for cross-backend test harness\\n- @dh:codebase-analyzer \u2014 for coupling surface area analysis\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n**Primary targets (modify):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/operations.py` \u2014 primary coupling point (~1400+ lines), needs backend DI refactor\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/gh_client.py` \u2014 GitHub API client, moves into GitHubBackend\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github_sync.py` \u2014 sync operations, moves into GitHubBackend\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/github_branches.py` \u2014 branch operations, moves into GitHubBackend\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/server.py` \u2014 40 MCP tool definitions, needs backend injection\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` \u2014 data models, may need backend-agnostic base types\\n\\n**New files (create):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` \u2014 ABC/Protocol definition\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/github.py` \u2014 GitHubBackend implementation\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/sqlite.py` \u2014 SQLiteBackend implementation (or alternative)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backends/__init__.py` \u2014 backend discovery/registry\\n\\n**Test files (47 files, 279 functions):**\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/` \u2014 existing test suite, needs fixture adaptation\\n- New: backend contract test suite covering all 40 tool operation groups\\n\\n**CI:**\\n- `.github/workflows/backlog-sync.yml` \u2014 needs backend env var configuration\\n\\n**Research references:**\\n- `research/task-management/beads.md` \u2014 Beads graph tracker research\\n- `research/agent-frameworks/get-shit-done.md` \u2014 GSD framework research\\n- `research/agent-frameworks/superpowers.md` \u2014 Superpowers framework research\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n**Upstream (blocks this work):**\\n- #329 \u2014 status unknown; original grooming referenced this as a dependency. Verify if still relevant or superseded by the gh_client.py/github_sync.py/github_branches.py split that already happened.\\n\\n**Downstream (blocked by this work):**\\n- Any future backend integration (GitLab, Jira, Beads) depends on the protocol being defined first\\n- Offline-mode backlog usage depends on SQLite backend\\n\\n**Cross-plugin awareness (not blocked, but affected):**\\n- python3-development plugin \u2014 imports backlog_core; public API must remain stable\\n- SAM sub-system \u2014 imports backlog_core; public API must remain stable\\n- These callers are NOT refactored in this item (see Scope anti-goals) but must be regression-tested\\n\\n**Research artifacts available:**\\n- research/task-management/beads.md (verified exists)\\n- research/agent-frameworks/get-shit-done.md\\n- research/agent-frameworks/superpowers.md\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\n**Estimate: Very High \u2014 multi-phase implementation recommended**\\n\\nOriginal estimate was \\\"High\\\" assuming 10 tools. With 40 tools across 5 operation groups, the effort is approximately 4x the original scope.\\n\\n**Recommended phasing:**\\n\\n**Phase 1 \u2014 Protocol + GitHub extraction (Large)**\\n- Define backend Protocol/ABC\\n- Extract GitHub-specific code from operations.py into GitHubBackend\\n- Wire dependency injection in server.py\\n- All 279 existing tests pass against GitHubBackend\\n- Estimated: 3-5 agent sessions\\n\\n**Phase 2 \u2014 Alternative backend (Medium)**\\n- Implement SQLiteBackend (or Beads)\\n- Backend-agnostic contract test suite\\n- Backend discovery mechanism\\n- Estimated: 2-3 agent sessions\\n\\n**Phase 3 \u2014 Integration + CI (Small)**\\n- Update backlog-sync.yml\\n- Cross-plugin regression testing\\n- Documentation\\n- Estimated: 1-2 agent sessions\\n\\n**Total: 6-10 agent sessions across 3 phases**\\n\\nPhasing de-risks the work: Phase 1 delivers the abstraction with zero behavioral change (GitHub backend only). Phase 2 proves the abstraction works. Phase 3 integrates.\\n\\n### Decision\\n\\n**RT-ICA: APPROVED**\\n\\nAll MISSING conditions identified by RT-ICA are deliverables of this item, not external blockers. The work can proceed.\\n\\n**Key findings from grooming swarm:**\\n1. Scope is 4x original \u2014 40 MCP tools (not 10), across 5 operation groups\\n2. github.py no longer exists \u2014 was split into gh_client.py + github_sync.py + github_branches.py\\n3. Test count is 279 functions in 47 files (not 382+)\\n4. Cross-plugin callers (python3-development, SAM) create additional risk surface\\n5. Impact analysis: HIGH risk, 65 systems, 45 with confirmed dependencies\\n\\n**Recommendation:** Accept as P1 (upgraded from P2) with mandatory phasing. Phase 1 (protocol + GitHub extraction) is self-contained and delivers the core abstraction. Do not attempt all 40 tools in a single pass.\\n\\n**Open question:** Verify #329 status \u2014 if the gh_client.py split already resolved what #329 was tracking, close it as superseded.\\n\\n### In Scope\\n\\n1. **Backend protocol/interface** \u2014 define abstract interface that all 40 MCP tools can call through\\n2. **GitHub backend extraction** \u2014 move GitHub-specific code from operations.py into a GitHubBackend implementation using gh_client.py + github_sync.py + github_branches.py\\n3. **Backend discovery/configuration** \u2014 mechanism to select backend at startup (env var, config file)\\n4. **All 40 MCP tools** \u2014 backlog (add/list/view/sync/close/resolve/groom/update/normalize/pull/strike/comment/search), dispatch (6 tools), artifact (5 tools), SAM (7 tools), profile (2 tools) \u2014 all must route through the backend protocol\\n5. **Test suite adaptation** \u2014 279 existing tests continue passing; add backend-agnostic test contract suite\\n6. **CI update** \u2014 .github/workflows/backlog-sync.yml updated with backend configuration\\n7. **At least one alternative backend** \u2014 SQLite or Beads (research at research/task-management/beads.md) proving the abstraction works\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\nIssue Classification: Abstract GitHub Issues layer from backlog MCP server into pluggable backend\\nType: unbounded-design\\nRationale: The backlog system works correctly for its current GitHub Issues backend \u2014 this is not a defect. The request introduces new capability (multi-backend support) that does not exist today. The scope is unbounded without design framing: what does the backend protocol look like? Which operations must every backend support? What is the error contract? Which backend ships second to validate the abstraction? These are design decisions that must be resolved before implementation can begin.\\nAnalysis Method: design-framing\\nScenario Target: User wants to use backlog system with a non-GitHub backend (GitLab, Jira, Beads, SQLite) \u2192 All 10+ MCP tools work identically against any conforming backend without changes to server.py or skill workflows\\n\\nDesign Framing:\\n1. Protocol boundary \u2014 Define the abstract interface (Python Protocol class or ABC) that every backend must implement. Operations: add, list, view, update, groom, close, resolve, sync, normalize, pull, strike, comment, labels, milestones, projects, artifacts.\\n2. Contract surface \u2014 Each operation needs defined input/output types, error semantics (what does \\\"not found\\\" look like?), and capability negotiation (not all backends support labels or milestones).\\n3. Validation criterion \u2014 The abstraction is correct when a second backend (e.g., SQLite or YAML-only local) passes the same test suite as the GitHub backend without modifying server.py.\\n4. Migration path \u2014 Existing GitHub backend must be refactored into the first conforming implementation with zero behavioral change to current users.\\n\\n### Out of Scope (Anti-Goals)\\n\\n- **Cross-plugin caller migration** \u2014 python3-development and SAM sub-system callers are NOT refactored in this item. They continue using the existing public API. The abstraction is internal to backlog_core.\\n- **MCP tool signature changes** \u2014 all 40 tool signatures remain identical. This is a backend swap, not an API redesign.\\n- **Data migration tooling** \u2014 no automated migration between backends (e.g., GitHub \u2192 SQLite). Manual export/import is acceptable for v1.\\n- **Backend feature parity guarantees** \u2014 alternative backends may not support every GitHub-specific feature (labels, milestones). Document gaps, don't block on them.\\n- **Performance optimization** \u2014 correctness first. Performance tuning is follow-on work.\\n\\n## Verification Results 2026 04 01\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n### Claim 1: \\\"10 MCP tools in the backlog server\\\"\\n**REFUTED** \u2014 Found 40 actual @mcp.tool-decorated functions in server.py, not 10.\\n- Tools: backlog_add, backlog_list, backlog_view, backlog_sync, backlog_close, backlog_resolve, backlog_update, backlog_groom, backlog_normalize, backlog_pull, backlog_comment_issue, backlog_list_comments, backlog_read_comment, backlog_list_issues, backlog_list_milestones, backlog_list_projects, backlog_create_milestone, backlog_create_project, backlog_create_sam_task, backlog_get_sam_tasks, backlog_get_ready_sam_tasks, backlog_update_sam_task_status, dispatch_read, dispatch_validate, dispatch_stale_check, dispatch_create_plan, dispatch_wave_start, dispatch_wave_status, dispatch_item_status, dispatch_spawn, artifact_register, artifact_list, artifact_get, artifact_read, artifact_migrate, profile_list, profile_load, sam_create, sam_list, sam_read, sam_state, sam_ready, sam_update, sam_claim (40 total)\\n\\n### Claim 2: \\\"382+ tests (or 380)\\\"\\n**REFUTED** \u2014 Actual test function count is 279, not 382. Grep count across plugins/development-harness/tests/ confirms 279 def test_ patterns.\\n\\n### Claim 3: \\\"Every operation assumes GitHub Issues API\\\"\\n**VERIFIED** \u2014 operations.py imports directly from github (PyGithub), .gh_client, and .github_sync. GitHub coupling is tight and verified.\\n\\n### Claim 4: \\\"github.py is the primary GitHub client wrapper (~268 lines)\\\"\\n**REFUTED** \u2014 github.py does not exist. Replaced by modularized components: gh_client.py (69.8KB), github_sync.py (16.7KB), github_branches.py (11.9KB).\\n\\n### Claim 5: \\\"Beads research documentation at research/task-management/beads.md\\\"\\n**VERIFIED** \u2014 File exists as of 2026-04-01.\\n\\n### Claim 6: \\\"Same 10 MCP tools work against any conforming backend with zero changes to server.py\\\"\\n**REFUTED** \u2014 Tool count is 40, not 10. Original scope claim is invalid. Backend abstraction feasibility cannot be assessed based on the wrong baseline.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact On Item Scope\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe original grooming estimated \\\"10 MCP tools\\\" as the scope for abstraction. The actual count (40 tools) is **4x larger** than estimated. This significantly expands the scope of the abstraction work:\\n- 40 tool signatures to refactor, not 10\\n- 40 backend interface contracts to define\\n- 40 integration points to test against multiple backends\\n\\nTest coverage (279 tests) is lower than grooming estimated (382), suggesting gaps in test breadth for the current tool set.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Recommendation\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThis item needs scope re-estimation based on verified tool count (40, not 10). Current grooming assumptions are no longer valid. Proceed with caution \u2014 the backend abstraction is a significantly larger task than originally estimated.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Artifact Manifest\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:begin -->\\n| Type | Path | Status | Agent | Created |\\n|------|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| feature-context | plan/feature-context-abstract-github-issues-layer-backlog-mcp.md | current | discovery | 2026-04-01T15:35:31.856457+00:00 |\\n| codebase-analysis | plan/codebase/architecture.md | current | codebase-analyzer | 2026-04-01T15:59:26.817149+00:00 |\\n| codebase-analysis | plan/codebase/testing.md | current | codebase-analyzer | 2026-04-01T15:59:52.996380+00:00 |\\n| architect | plan/architect-abstract-github-issues-layer-backlog-mcp.md | current | python-cli-design-spec | 2026-04-01T16:04:50.150251+00:00 |\\n| task-plan | plan/P389-backlog-pluggable-backend.yaml | current |  | 2026-04-01T16:16:56Z |\\n| T0-baseline | plan/T0-baseline-backlog-pluggable-backend.yaml | current | t0-baseline-capture | 2026-04-01T16:47:51.239174+00:00 |\\n| TN-verification | plan/TN-verification-backlog-pluggable-backend.yaml | current | tn-verification-gate | 2026-04-01T18:42:07.610868+00:00 |\\n<!-- artifact-manifest:end -->\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"f800b0ac4e261fa9a28e61c0b6b764a6f2eff616ac8297fbf4e58d1ea899cb2d\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVWQrOg\"}"}